      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the \"audio entrainment\" thing might be a logical way to look at it, but it doesn't explain why the machine itself wasn't even vibrating. it was just... a sound coming from a static object. it felt like a low-res audio asset being played on a loop.\n\nthe pressure thing is what's really messing with me though. it wasn't just a feeling, it felt like a physical weight, like the local simulation was drawing so much processing power to try and fix that audio glitch that the frame rate of my own sensory input actually dropped. have u ever seen any data points or logs that suggest sudden spikes in local processing loads coinciding with environmental anomalies? like a sudden dip in stability?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
